# What P15's review found in the shell and its commands (roadmap
# os-server.md P15): an unquoted expansion of nothing is no word; \" in a
# double quote ends nothing, for the lists' split too; cp of a file onto
# itself is refused, not emptied; cp takes a DOS path's last name after
# its drive; sleep refuses what would wrap; sh reads a file of commands a
# byte at a time, no line's start lost, and without a prompt or an echo
# (P15's second review).
program: sh
install: C /BIN/CP z-cp.rx
install: C /BIN/SLEEP z-sleep.rx
keys: echo a $EMPTY b; echo "say \\"hi; bye\\""; echo "a\\"b" && echo two\n
keys: cd /mnt/rx286b; echo hello > s.txt; cp s.txt s.txt; echo [$?]; cat s.txt\n
keys: cp c:readme.txt /mnt/rx286b; ls /mnt/rx286b/readme.txt; sleep 65536; echo [$?]\n
keys: echo echo first > /mnt/rx286b/s; echo echo second >> /mnt/rx286b/s; echo echo third >> /mnt/rx286b/s; sh < /mnt/rx286b/s\n
---
rx286, test build
/mnt/rx286$ echo a $EMPTY b; echo "say \"hi; bye\""; echo "a\"b" && echo two
a b
say "hi; bye"
a"b
two
/mnt/rx286$ cd /mnt/rx286b; echo hello > s.txt; cp s.txt s.txt; echo [$?]; cat s.txt
cp: a file onto itself
[1]
hello
/mnt/rx286b$ cp c:readme.txt /mnt/rx286b; ls /mnt/rx286b/readme.txt; sleep 65536; echo [$?]
/mnt/rx286b/readme.txt
usage: sleep SECONDS
[1]
/mnt/rx286b$ echo echo first > /mnt/rx286b/s; echo echo second >> /mnt/rx286b/s; echo echo third >> /mnt/rx286b/s; sh < /mnt/rx286b/s
first
second
third
/mnt/rx286b$
